ue "2x\\ln x+x+\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186576147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddbe9744-04e5-5a13-898b-3293efe4160f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}+3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571233} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6a34341-fe46-5049-b63f-03fb79ef67af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f475b19b-1e35-517e-8f15-4fa3d740b6ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-320824" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=({x}^{2}+3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}+3$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2}+3)}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+({x}^{2}+3){(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))}^{′} \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))+({x}^{2}+3)\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+\\frac{{x}^{2}+3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186586552 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e9a10c-b454-5d9e-b42d-a5b4e64d2a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3^x\\ln(3)\\cos(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04e9a10c-b454-5d9e-b42d-a5b4e64d2a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3^x\\ln(3)\\cos(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585886} :answer-field/id #uuid "517709e9-f87f-51ef-86e5-3a7246853549" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 1