 :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}}{2\\sqrt{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586226} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c400dff-bed5-5d41-986f-72a99df176f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186586417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64d86353-289c-5c4c-a5f5-b6e2b66703e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-47954" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}{e}^{x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\sqrt{x})^{′}\\cdot {e}^{x}+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}{e}^{x}+\\sqrt{x}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}+2x{e}^{x}}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0847027d-bd26-57f8-9403-9e4eb6cdf358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(11\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657611} {:answer/id #uuid "3e3cc552-b13d-5424-9879-4f15ac541649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(10\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657615} {:answer/id #uuid "921c17d0-1976-5b3a-915c-86d80055277b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(8\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657621} {:answer/id #uuid "96e424aa-4e93-575f-89d4-05f0f2353484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657622} {:answer/id #uuid "bffd7eb9-1ef0-5aae-98d8-18005e448afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(9\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e424aa-4e93-575f-89d4-05f0f2353484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(12\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657622} :answer-field/id #uuid "571e7da4-8bf0-538e-b7aa-3f10b987cbb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186657617}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bcc9f93-4f3c-5124-8641-edf082f5099b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = 6\\log_{5} x\\ln x$, find $f^{′}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=6\\log_{5} x$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(6\\log_{5} x)^{′}\\ln x+6\\log_{5} x(\\ln x)^{′} \\\\  & =(\\frac{6}{x \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}})(\\ln x)+(6\\log_{5} x)(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\log_{5} x}{x} + \\frac{6\\ln x}{x\\ln 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186657613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a5691a-21e3-5308-8cb3-fbdd26bcd3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(-2\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{3} \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{3} \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/